WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:08.189
We’ve only been able to record sound for
just over 150 years but in that time we have

00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:13.700
done some amazing things with sound, and captured
some amazing historical events.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:21.860
Here’s a rundown of some of the creepiest
and most chilling sounds ever recorded.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:25.779
1.

00:00:25.779 --> 00:00:34.500
Sound recording was invented in 1857 by Édouard-Léon
Scott de Martinville when he created the Phonautograph.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:39.680
It was used to create the first ever sound
recording, which is believed to be the inventor

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:55.100
himself, singing “Au clair de la lune”
in 1860.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:01:00.560
By today’s audio standards it’s a very
creepy sounding recording, and being over

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:04.830
154 years old, is an imperative piece of history.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:05.830
2.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:11.740
In the early 1960s the space race was on between
the United States and the Soviet Union.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:17.190
The competition between the two nations was
fierce and whoever successfully made it into

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:21.420
space first would forever have bragging rights.

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:27.310
The American tragedies that ensued as a result
of their attempts to reach space are well

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:28.310
known.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:31.880
But the Soviet Unions’ not so much.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:38.460
At the time many amateur radio enthusiasts
were building home-brew radio equipment at

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:44.150
home that allowed them to listen into space
communication frequencies used by the two

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:46.180
nations during their voyages.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:53.490
Two brothers in Turin, Italy named Achille
and Giovanni Judica-Cordiglia were way ahead

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:58.450
of most people in this field with their radio
and telecommunications equipment.

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:06.940
They were able to tune in to all the Soviet
Union’s space frequencies and record their

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:08.019
transmissions.

00:02:08.019 --> 00:02:12.920
In May of 1961 the two brothers picked up
a transmission from a Soviet Space frequency

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.500
that chilled them to their core.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:19.950
It was the voice of a female, clearly in distress.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:36.380
This is a short clip of the actual recording
made by the brothers.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:40.730
The woman is speaking in Russian but when
translated she is saying:

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:41.890
“I feel hot.

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:43.349
I can see a flame.

00:02:43.349 --> 00:02:45.270
Am I going to crash?

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:47.250
Yes, yes, I will reenter”

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:51.820
And then the transmission cuts out.

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:57.540
Three days after the recording was made the
official Soviet news agency, TASS announced

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:01.500
a failed reentry of a satellite the size of
a bus.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:07.250
However the launch had not been previously
announced and the satellite was never mentioned

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:08.930
to anyone.

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:14.700
To this day the Soviet Union has never acknowledged
the alleged incident and the identity of the

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.840
woman still remains completely unknown.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:18.840
3.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:25.840
At number 3 is a 1922 recording made by Thomas
Edison of Harry E. Humphrey.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:32.040
Edison recorded it on his own invention the
phonograph, which was the very first audio

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.040
player.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:37.680
The idea was to sell the recording to owners
of Edison’s phonograph so that they could

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:41.770
play it to their Children and experience Christmas
Joy.

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:49.040
But it had the opposite effect, in fact it’s
just about the most terrifying Christmas message

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.570
you will ever hear.

00:03:50.570 --> 00:04:32.720
Here’s a short clip from the original recording:

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:38.400
The laugh alone is enough to put kids off
Father Christmas forever.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.479
4.

00:04:40.479 --> 00:04:43.270
Saturn is a source of intense radio emissions.

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:49.300
In 2002 when the Cassini spacecraft did a
flyby of Saturn it recorded these strange

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:52.919
radio emissions emanating from Saturn.

00:04:52.919 --> 00:04:58.009
If you listen closely you can hear what appears
to be an alien voice.

00:04:58.009 --> 00:05:12.960
It 

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:17.689
is very hard to make out any words yet some
people believe believed they have deciphered

00:05:17.689 --> 00:05:24.400
the message as this: “You people are urged
to drop the Earthly Impulse”.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:28.159
What do you think, is it aliens or just gargled
space static?

00:05:28.159 --> 00:05:29.159
5.

00:05:29.159 --> 00:05:34.539
Operation Wandering Soul was an attempt by
the US military during the Vietnamese war

00:05:34.539 --> 00:05:39.449
to scare the opposition into submission by
playing terrifying sounds through the jungle

00:05:39.449 --> 00:05:41.530
in the dead of night.

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:46.849
It is the Vietnamese belief that the dead
must be buried in their homeland, or their

00:05:46.849 --> 00:05:50.289
soul will wander aimlessly in pain and suffering.

00:05:50.289 --> 00:05:55.569
Therefore when they heard the following sound
echoing out from the depths of the dense jungle.

00:05:55.569 --> 00:06:09.460
They would have certainly felt a great sense
of turmoil and dread.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:25.539
The US militants would often broadcast the
sound from loudspeaker systems aboard helicopters.

00:06:25.539 --> 00:06:26.539
6.

00:06:26.539 --> 00:06:32.259
During the Cold War for over 30 years the
shortwave radio spectrum was used by the world’s

00:06:32.259 --> 00:06:38.819
intelligence agencies to transmit secret messages
to their spies who were stationed in enemy

00:06:38.819 --> 00:06:39.819
countries.

00:06:39.819 --> 00:06:44.680
These transmissions were called numbers stations
and were completely anonymous, one-way radio

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:51.080
transmissions across shortwave radio that
could be picked up and listened too by anyone,

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:54.839
using only very basic radio equipment.

00:06:54.839 --> 00:07:01.180
Numbers stations were broadcast 24 hours a
day on very rigid schedules by various European

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:02.180
countries.

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:07.240
The broadcasts were nothing more than female
or male voices repeating a series of numbers

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:08.619
and letters.

00:07:08.619 --> 00:07:14.029
The key feature of these broadcasts is that
the coded messages they contain are completely

00:07:14.029 --> 00:07:19.979
unbreakable and can only be understood by
the select few whom are supposed to receive

00:07:19.979 --> 00:07:21.630
the message.

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:27.999
Despite many attempts, nobody apart from the
intended recipient has ever been able to decode

00:07:27.999 --> 00:07:30.229
a numbers station message.

00:07:30.229 --> 00:07:44.419
This is a recording of a British numbers station
transmission.

00:07:44.419 --> 00:08:01.099
And this is a German station, known by radio
enthusiasts as the Swedish Rhapsody.

00:08:01.099 --> 00:08:14.360
It uniquely features a really creepy little
girl.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:29.189
There’s a bizarre numbers station called
the “Backwards Music Station”, because

00:08:29.189 --> 00:08:33.090
some believe it sounds like music being played
backwards.

00:08:33.090 --> 00:08:38.090
The signal is believed to be transmitted from
both the US and UK.

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:43.260
The difference between this numbers station
and most others is that it never plays any

00:08:43.260 --> 00:09:08.140
voice messages, just endless, hellish noises.

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:13.080
One would think that numbers stations would
have died out at the end of the Cold War around

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:14.080
1991.

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:21.190
But they are still widely used by intelligence
agencies today, to transmit messages to spies,

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:26.870
because shortwave radio still remains a very
reliable means of communication.

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:33.840
So if you tune into the right frequencies
at the right time you may hear a live broadcast

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:35.890
of a real numbers station.

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:36.890
7.

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:41.550
If your picture of space is a vast, silent
nothingness dotted with weird looking rocks

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:44.660
you would be half-wrong.

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:49.591
Space is silent to the human ear, but with
the right equipment you can pick up and record

00:09:49.591 --> 00:09:51.750
vibrations in space.

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:58.070
This is exactly what happened when NASA’s
Voyager spacecraft recorded Jupiter’s atmosphere,

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:11.500
this is the sound it picked up.

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:27.800
It’s incredibly eerie to think that such
a sound can be made by a planet.

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:32.310
It sounds more like an alien tractor beam
than a big ball of gas.

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:36.890
The sound is actually a result of the complex
interactions of charged electromagnetic particles

00:10:36.890 --> 00:10:39.230
in the planet’s solar winds and magnetosphere.

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:42.970
And you thought playing an instrument was
complicated.

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:43.970
8.

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:47.520
Speaking of space, not all space noises come
from planets.

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:54.860
In 1977 The Big Ear radio telescope at The
Ohio State University picked up a narrowband

00:10:54.860 --> 00:11:12.460
radio signal from outer space that sounded
like this.

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:18.040
It was named the Wow signal because the man
who first spotted it on the logs circled it

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:21.530
in red pen and wrote Wow beside it.

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:27.480
But the peculiar thing about the Wow signal
is that it came from a location in outer space

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:33.800
that contains no planets or galaxies, a seemingly
empty area of space.

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:38.720
So how could a signal be transmitted from
an area of complete nothingness.

00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:46.760
Unless it wasn’t actually empty, many people
believe the signal came from an alien spacecraft

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:50.920
travelling through the vast emptiness of outer
space.

00:11:50.920 --> 00:12:00.680
To this day science still can’t explain
where the signal originated from.

